# Where the deploy job has wrangler write its structured output, so the version
# id and preview URL can be read as data rather than scraped from console text.
.wrangler-output/

# Agent tooling. Local to whoever is working here, not part of the site: it
# describes how to work on the project rather than what the project is, and its
# infrastructure half still documented a Docker and nginx deployment that no
# longer exists. Keeping it out of version control means it cannot go stale in
# the repo, and cannot mislead someone who trusts a checked-in document.
.agents/
.claude/
skills-lock.json
